          <p>
            If you can edit HTML, you can maintain this blog. The homepage lists recent posts; each post is a
            separate file; <code>feed.xml</code> is a static Atom feed you can update when you publish.
          </p>

          <p>
            Host it anywhere that serves files: object storage with a CDN, GitHub Pages, Neocities, or your own
            web server. No build step required.
          </p>

          <blockquote>
            <p>The goal is durability: fewer moving parts means fewer things to break.</p>
          </blockquote>

          <p><a href="../index.html">Home</a></p>
